    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d955">

                <pb facs="1456" n="1442" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 E.W./10–1844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-18T17:00:00+01:00">October 18, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>178.<anchor n="68" xml:id="d955-f1"/> “I am instructed by the Secretary of State
                    to inform you that (1) The American Government has carefully studied the Irish
                    Government’s <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> dated October 9,
                        1944<anchor n="69" xml:id="d955-f2"/> in reply to the request of the
                    American Government for assurances as to Axis war criminals embodied in our <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> dated September 21, 1944;<anchor
                        n="70" xml:id="d955-f3"/> (2) The American Government notes that the Irish
                    Government does not vouchsafe the assurances requested and regrets that the
                    Irish Government does not choose to exercise its sovereignty in unequivocal and
                    sympathetic cooperation with the United Nations in proclaiming denial of asylum
                    to Axis war criminals responsible for the horrors that have shocked the
                    civilized world.”</p>
                <p>Repeated to London as No. 58.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
